    "rationale": "The culture plateaus at an OD of about 0.42 from 6 h onward. Diluted reads scale back to the undiluted value. At 18 h, a 10x dilution read 0.0432, which gives 0.43 against 0.42 undiluted. At 12 h, a 4x dilution read 0.117, which gives 0.47 against 0.43 undiluted. The 12 h value is slightly higher, but replicate scatter of about 0.005 per read, scaled by 4, covers the difference. A saturated or non-linear reading would give a clearly higher diluted OD, and that did not appear. The plateau therefore looks like genuine stationary phase."
